Paper batch 2 of round 3: block U upsert cells (U3, U4) and Claude Sonnet 5.5 as definition-item writer (H1, H2) judged and written into the paper

Stage runs/stage7_round3 again from the raw runs (analysis code b765491, clean): u.json holds the
refresh and upsert runs of block U (U1/U2 values unchanged), h_sonnet.json block H for the Claude
Sonnet 5.5 definition-item writer read with its response-cache snapshot (SHA256 in the manifest),
u_delta.json the exploratory upsert split; n.json and y.json differ only in the code field. Commit
the manifests, env and hash checks of the seven upsert and five H-a runs. RThree macros and
tab_round3 regenerated; tests pin the staged verdicts and values.

Verdicts: U3 judged, reading key_schedule (R_upsert pooled 0.01 [-0.02, 0.04]); U4 fails (S_del,
all items, D=1: -2.8 pp [-4.3, -1.4]); U5 not judged (M2 families not run). H-a valid (944
distinct writes, 0 at the output limit, 0 unreadable); H1 reads both (B x D after S_def +16.4 pp
[+9.7, +22.4]); H2 holds (r_0 45.5% [36.0, 53.1], +32.7 pp [+26.6, +38.5] over Qwen3.5-9B on the
same item-times). Exploratory: at D=1 the delta yielded no new item on 27% and 36% of the changed
definition item-times after S_src and S_def, which carry 79% and 93% of binding's effect; the upsert
changed 4 answers on definition items and 120 on the other items.

Paper: abstract and introduction state the upsert and the frontier-writer result; 4.1 gives the
upsert next to the refresh with the delta mechanism; 4.2 adds the Claude writer; 4.4 the U4 failure;
rule 2, the Models and Construct limitations, the reproducibility statement and appendix B (models,
round-3 subsection, status, readings and deviations tables) updated; detail moved to the appendix
and prose compressed so the main text still ends on page 9.

